@page "/platform"
@attribute [AllowAnonymous]
@layout MarketingLayout
@rendermode InteractiveServer
@inject NavigationManager Nav

<PageTitle>Platform: What HIP Measures | HIP</PageTitle>
<HeadContent>
  <meta name="description" content="The six signal families behind a HIP score: connection and certificates, DNS and ownership, domain reputation, page behaviour, wording patterns, and independent provider results." />
  <meta property="og:title" content="Platform: What HIP Measures | HIP" />
  <meta property="og:description" content="The six signal families behind a HIP score: connection and certificates, DNS and ownership, domain reputation, page behaviour, wording patterns, and independent provider results." />
  <meta property="og:url" content="https://guardwithhip.com/platform" />
  <meta property="og:image" content="https://guardwithhip.com/images/public/marketing/og-image.png" />
  <link rel="canonical" href="https://guardwithhip.com/platform" />
</HeadContent>

<main style="max-width:1240px;margin:0 auto;padding:clamp(56px,6vw,80px) clamp(16px,3vw,32px) 110px">
  <div style="max-width:680px;margin-bottom:64px">
    <div style="font-size:12px;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:.2em;color:var(--action);margin-bottom:16px">PLATFORM</div>
    <h1 style="font-size:clamp(36px,4.6vw,52px);line-height:1.06;letter-spacing:-.03em;font-weight:800;margin:0 0 18px;text-wrap:balance">Six signal families, one readable score.</h1>
    <p style="font-size:19px;line-height:1.6;color:var(--muted);margin:0;text-wrap:pretty">HIP does not guess at intent. It measures things that can be checked, weights them with rules anyone can read, and shows the arithmetic.</p>
  </div>

  <div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(340px,1fr));gap:20px;margin-bottom:80px">
    <div style="background:var(--surface);border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:18px;padding:32px">
      <div style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:12px;margin-bottom:16px"><span style="font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace;font-size:12px;font-weight:700;color:var(--action)">01</span><h3 style="font-size:21px;font-weight:700;margin:0;letter-spacing:-.015em">Transport &amp; certificates</h3></div>
      <p style="font-size:15.5px;line-height:1.65;color:var(--muted);margin:0 0 18px">Does the site force HTTPS? Are redirects clean? Is the certificate valid, from a trusted issuer, and not about to expire? Weak transport is a common and often fixable website problem.</p>
      <div style="display:flex;gap:7px;flex-wrap:wrap"><span style="padding:5px 11px;border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:999px;font-size:12px;color:var(--muted);font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace">https.enforced</span><span style="padding:5px 11px;border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:999px;font-size:12px;color:var(--muted);font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace">tls.version</span><span style="padding:5px 11px;border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:999px;font-size:12px;color:var(--muted);font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace">cert.expiry</span></div>
    </div>
    <div style="background:var(--surface);border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:18px;padding:32px">
      <div style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:12px;margin-bottom:16px"><span style="font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace;font-size:12px;font-weight:700;color:var(--action)">02</span><h3 style="font-size:21px;font-weight:700;margin:0;letter-spacing:-.015em">DNS &amp; ownership</h3></div>
      <p style="font-size:15.5px;line-height:1.65;color:var(--muted);margin:0 0 18px">Record configuration, mail-authentication posture, and a TXT-record proof that ties a domain to the person managing it. Verification is what separates a scan from a claim.</p>
      <div style="display:flex;gap:7px;flex-wrap:wrap"><span style="padding:5px 11px;border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:999px;font-size:12px;color:var(--muted);font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace">dns.records</span><span style="padding:5px 11px;border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:999px;font-size:12px;color:var(--muted);font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace">mail.auth</span><span style="padding:5px 11px;border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:999px;font-size:12px;color:var(--muted);font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace">owner.txt</span></div>
    </div>
    <div style="background:var(--surface);border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:18px;padding:32px">
      <div style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:12px;margin-bottom:16px"><span style="font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace;font-size:12px;font-weight:700;color:var(--action)">03</span><h3 style="font-size:21px;font-weight:700;margin:0;letter-spacing:-.015em">Domain reputation</h3></div>
      <p style="font-size:15.5px;line-height:1.65;color:var(--muted);margin:0 0 18px">Age, history, hosting context and third-party listings. A brand-new domain is not automatically bad. It carries less evidence, and the score says so clearly.</p>
      <div style="display:flex;gap:7px;flex-wrap:wrap"><span style="padding:5px 11px;border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:999px;font-size:12px;color:var(--muted);font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace">domain.age</span><span style="padding:5px 11px;border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:999px;font-size:12px;color:var(--muted);font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace">listings</span></div>
    </div>
    <div style="background:var(--surface);border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:18px;padding:32px">
      <div style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:12px;margin-bottom:16px"><span style="font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace;font-size:12px;font-weight:700;color:var(--action)">04</span><h3 style="font-size:21px;font-weight:700;margin:0;letter-spacing:-.015em">Page behaviour</h3></div>
      <p style="font-size:15.5px;line-height:1.65;color:var(--muted);margin:0 0 18px">Where forms post to, what third parties load, whether credentials are requested over insecure channels, and whether the page tries to obscure what it is doing.</p>
      <div style="display:flex;gap:7px;flex-wrap:wrap"><span style="padding:5px 11px;border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:999px;font-size:12px;color:var(--muted);font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace">form.targets</span><span style="padding:5px 11px;border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:999px;font-size:12px;color:var(--muted);font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace">third.party</span><span style="padding:5px 11px;border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:999px;font-size:12px;color:var(--muted);font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace">obfuscation</span></div>
    </div>
    <div style="background:var(--surface);border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:18px;padding:32px">
      <div style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:12px;margin-bottom:16px"><span style="font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace;font-size:12px;font-weight:700;color:var(--action)">05</span><h3 style="font-size:21px;font-weight:700;margin:0;letter-spacing:-.015em">Wording &amp; pressure patterns</h3></div>
      <p style="font-size:15.5px;line-height:1.65;color:var(--muted);margin:0 0 18px">Language that manufactures urgency, impersonates a provider, or pushes for credentials. These rules are the most contestable, so HIP documents them openly and allows appeals.</p>
      <div style="display:flex;gap:7px;flex-wrap:wrap"><span style="padding:5px 11px;border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:999px;font-size:12px;color:var(--muted);font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace">urgency</span><span style="padding:5px 11px;border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:999px;font-size:12px;color:var(--muted);font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace">impersonation</span></div>
    </div>
    <div style="background:var(--surface);border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:18px;padding:32px">
      <div style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:12px;margin-bottom:16px"><span style="font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace;font-size:12px;font-weight:700;color:var(--action)">06</span><h3 style="font-size:21px;font-weight:700;margin:0;letter-spacing:-.015em">External provider results</h3></div>
      <p style="font-size:15.5px;line-height:1.65;color:var(--muted);margin:0 0 18px">SSL Labs, Google Safe Browsing and VirusTotal feed in as attributed signals. HIP records which provider said what, and when, so a verdict can be traced to its source.</p>
      <div style="display:flex;gap:7px;flex-wrap:wrap"><span style="padding:5px 11px;border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:999px;font-size:12px;color:var(--muted);font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace">provider.ssllabs</span><span style="padding:5px 11px;border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:999px;font-size:12px;color:var(--muted);font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace">provider.gsb</span></div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div style="background:var(--surface);border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:22px;padding:clamp(28px,3.4vw,48px);display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(340px,1fr));gap:52px;align-items:center">
    <div>
      <div style="font-size:12px;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:.2em;color:var(--action);margin-bottom:14px">SCORING</div>
      <h2 style="font-size:clamp(25px,2.8vw,32px);line-height:1.15;letter-spacing:-.025em;font-weight:800;margin:0 0 16px;text-wrap:balance">Rules you can read, argue with, and change.</h2>
      <p style="font-size:16.5px;line-height:1.65;color:var(--muted);margin:0 0 18px;text-wrap:pretty">Detection rules and their weights are plain configuration in the repository. Propose a change, discuss it in the open, and see the effect on real scans before it ships.</p>
      <p style="font-size:16.5px;line-height:1.65;color:var(--muted);margin:0">Every scored domain keeps an audit history: what changed, when, and which rule version produced it.</p>
    </div>
    <div style="background:var(--bg);border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:14px;padding:22px;font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace;font-size:12.5px;line-height:1.85;overflow:auto">
      <div style="color:var(--muted)"># rules/transport.yml</div>
      <div><span style="color:var(--violet)">id</span><span style="color:var(--muted)">:</span> https.not_enforced</div>
      <div><span style="color:var(--violet)">severity</span><span style="color:var(--muted)">:</span> <span style="color:var(--warn)">high</span></div>
      <div><span style="color:var(--violet)">weight</span><span style="color:var(--muted)">:</span> <span style="color:var(--action)">-18</span></div>
      <div><span style="color:var(--violet)">reason</span><span style="color:var(--muted)">:</span> "This site does not force a<br />&nbsp;&nbsp;secure connection, so visitors can<br />&nbsp;&nbsp;be served over plain HTTP."</div>
      <div><span style="color:var(--violet)">fix</span><span style="color:var(--muted)">:</span> "Redirect all HTTP traffic to<br />&nbsp;&nbsp;HTTPS and enable HSTS."</div>
      <div><span style="color:var(--violet)">appealable</span><span style="color:var(--muted)">:</span> <span style="color:var(--ok)">true</span></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</main>

<DomainTimeline />

<ScanPulse />

@code {
    private void GoScan() => Nav.NavigateTo("/#scan");
}
